Every morning, the town clock ran one minute late. The clockmaker replaced its hands, cleaned its gears, and checked it against his watch. Nothing helped. Then a child noticed the clock was perfectly accurate at midnight. The town had been moving its meeting time forward every morning, trying to start work sooner. By the end of the month, everyone arrived half an hour early and blamed the only clock that had never changed. So why did the town clock run one minute late every morning?